1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
From a knight's campsite to a train in the
sky,

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:07,320
let's explore eight creations their makers say
they built with Astra.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,920
First up is a little campsite where a knight
spends his day beside a fire.

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:14,080
He adds firewood, practices with his sword,

5
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:17,480
and cooks some meat. When he's tired, he lies
down to sleep.

6
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:21,100
It's not just about fighting. This knight gets
some downtime, too.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,800
Next is a train game set high in the sky.

8
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:40,860
Travel between floating islands and pick up
passengers at the station.

9
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,360
You can customize your train in the garage,
too.

10
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:46,860
I'm supposed to drive the train, but I'd
rather enjoy the view first.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,120
This creation is a virtual world where you can
decorate your own room and explore.

12
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:11,420
Place a desk and chair, change their colors,

13
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:15,780
then step inside. Head outdoors and you can
even go fishing.

14
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,420
I came to decorate a room and ended up
catching fish.

15
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,440
This post brings together four creations by
one maker.

16
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:37,320
There's a canal town full of moving residents,

17
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:39,940
and a game where you guide a ring without
touching a wire.

18
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:42,240
There's a chase game where you run from a
chef,

19
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:45,940
and a downhill game with a vehicle you
assemble yourself.

20
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:49,220
From a quiet stroll through town to narrowly
dodging obstacles,

21
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:51,040
each one has a different feel.

22
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,120
This one is about refining the look of a
little character.

23
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:17,100
The creator works on the colors of the clothes
and hair,

24
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:20,100
turning the model around to inspect awkward
spots.

25
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:24,460
There's still work to do, but you can see the
character coming together.

26
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:36,040
Here, the creator worked on colors and shadows
with a Zenless Zone Zero-inspired look.

27
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,280
This isn't about creating the character itself
from scratch,

28
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:40,840
but about how it appears in a game.

29
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:44,880
The close-ups of the face and outfit show off
those comic-like colors.

30
00:02:55,500 --> 00:03:00,100
The same creator also shared a character
rendering inspired by Endfield.

31
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:02,780
The demo shows the colors and shadows of the
hair and clothing,

32
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:05,580
turning the character to view it from
different angles.

33
00:03:05,980 --> 00:03:10,680
The colors can give a 3D character a very
different feel.

34
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:22,360
Finally, here's a city you can drive around.

35
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:27,500
The demo shows driving along the coast,
walking through the streets, and firing a gun.

36
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:30,380
With buildings, cars, and people all together,

37
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:34,120
it feels like visiting a neighborhood in a
game rather than a single small scene.

38
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:36,780
It makes me wonder what's around the next
corner.

39
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:52,420
From a little campsite to an entire city,
there's quite a range.

40
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:57,080
Which one would you like to try? Let me know
in the comments.
